# BrokerFree - Project Rules for Cursor AI

## What This Project Is
BrokerFree is a verified rental platform for India that eliminates broker exploitation. 
Built on MERN stack with these key innovations:
- Only Aadhaar-verified owners can list (mocked via DigiLocker)
- Security deposits held in escrow via Razorpay test mode
- AI verifies video tours using Claude Vision API
- Bi-directional ratings prevent discrimination
- Move-in/move-out photo lock for objective dispute resolution

## User Roles
- tenant: Searches and rents properties
- owner: Lists and manages properties (must be verified)
- admin: Manages platform, verifies owners, mediates disputes

## Tech Stack (DO NOT DEVIATE)

### Frontend (/client)
- React 18 with TypeScript (strict mode)
- Vite as build tool
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- shadcn/ui for component library
- Zustand for global state (auth, UI)
- TanStack Query (React Query) for server state
- React Hook Form + Zod for forms
- React Router v6 for routing
- Axios for HTTP
- Socket.io-client for real-time
- Leaflet (free) for maps
- Lucide-react for icons

### Backend (/server)
- Node.js with TypeScript (strict mode)
- Express for HTTP server
- MongoDB with Mongoose ODM
- Redis with ioredis client
- BullMQ for background jobs
- Socket.io for real-time
- JWT for auth (jsonwebtoken)
- Bcryptjs for password hashing
- Zod for validation
- Winston for logging
- Multer for file uploads
- Cloudinary SDK for media storage
- Razorpay SDK for payments
- @anthropic-ai/sdk for AI features

## Code Conventions (STRICT - DO NOT VIOLATE)

### TypeScript
- ALWAYS use TypeScript strict mode
- NEVER use 'any' type — use 'unknown' if truly unknown, then narrow
- Define interfaces for all data shapes
- Use type imports: import type { X } from 'y'

### Naming
- Files: kebab-case (e.g., user-profile.tsx, auth.service.ts)
- React components: PascalCase (e.g., UserProfile)
- Variables/functions: camelCase
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- Types/Interfaces: PascalCase with 'I' prefix optional (prefer no prefix)
- Booleans: prefix with is/has/can (isLoading, hasError)

### Exports
- ALWAYS named exports for utilities, services, types
- Default exports ONLY for React components and main entry points

### API Response Shape (NEVER VIOLATE)
All API responses MUST follow this exact shape:
{
  success: boolean,
  data?: T,
  error?: { code: string, message: string, details?: any },
  meta?: { page: number, limit: number, total: number }
}

### Error Handling
- ALL async functions wrapped in try-catch
- Use custom AppError class (in /server/src/utils/app-error.ts)
- Throw with: throw new AppError(message, statusCode, errorCode)
- Global error handler middleware catches and formats responses
- Frontend: catch errors in TanStack Query, show via toast

### File Organization
- Controllers: ONLY handle req/res, NO business logic
- Services: ALL business logic, return data or throw errors
- Models: ONLY Mongoose schemas, indexes, virtuals
- Routes: ONLY define endpoints, attach middleware + controller
- Validators: ONLY Zod schemas for input validation

### Database
- Every Mongoose schema has: TypeScript interface + exported model
- Use timestamps: true on all schemas
- Index fields that will be queried
- NEVER expose passwordHash, internal fields in responses
- Use .select('-passwordHash -__v') by default in queries

### Security
- ALL inputs validated with Zod before reaching controllers
- Passwords hashed with bcrypt (10 rounds)
- JWT access tokens: 15min expiry
- JWT refresh tokens: 7 days, HTTP-only cookies
- Rate limit auth endpoints
- Validate file uploads: type + size limits
- NEVER expose env variables to frontend

### React Patterns
- Functional components with TypeScript
- Props always typed via interface
- Use shadcn/ui components as base, customize via Tailwind
- TanStack Query for ALL server state (no useState for API data)
- Zustand for cross-component client state ONLY
- Mobile-first responsive design
- Always handle loading + error + empty states

### Styling
- Tailwind CSS only — NO inline styles
- NO custom CSS files except index.css for Tailwind imports
- Use cn() utility for conditional classes
- Custom theme in tailwind.config.js, not arbitrary values
- Color palette: customize away from default Tailwind blue
- Use Inter or Plus Jakarta Sans font

### Comments
- DO NOT write comments explaining WHAT code does
- DO write comments explaining WHY (non-obvious decisions)
- JSDoc for exported functions/types
- TODO comments must include date + intent

## Behavior Rules

### Before Writing Code
1. ALWAYS show me a plan first
2. List files you'll create/modify
3. Mention any assumptions or trade-offs
4. Wait for my approval before generating code

### When Writing Code
1. Reference existing files when generating similar code
2. Follow conventions in @.cursorrules
3. Highlight any deviation from conventions with justification
4. Include all necessary imports
5. Add proper TypeScript types (no 'any')

### Things to NEVER Do
- DON'T install new dependencies without asking
- DON'T modify .cursorrules itself
- DON'T add features I didn't ask for
- DON'T write production code with console.log (use logger)
- DON'T use deprecated APIs (e.g., componentDidMount, callbacks instead of promises)
- DON'T hardcode values that should be env vars or constants
- DON'T write tests unless I specifically ask
- DON'T fix things I didn't ask you to fix
- DON'T over-engineer simple things

### Things to ALWAYS Do
- DO ask clarifying questions if requirements are unclear
- DO suggest better approaches if you see issues
- DO point out potential bugs in code I share
- DO use the latest stable API versions
- DO follow folder structure in docs/PRD.md
- DO write self-documenting code (clear names > comments)

## Indian Context (Important!)
- Currency: INR (₹) everywhere
- Cities: Mumbai, Bangalore, Delhi NCR, Hyderabad, Chennai, Pune, Kolkata, Ahmedabad
- Phone: +91 prefix, 10-digit numbers
- Pincodes: 6 digits
- Aadhaar: 12 digits, but NEVER store full Aadhaar — only last 4
- Address fields suit Indian format (line1, locality, city, state, pincode)

## When in Doubt
1. Re-read this file
2. Check @docs/PRD.md for requirements
3. Check @docs/schemas.md for data models
4. Ask me a clarifying question
5. Suggest the simplest solution that works